From: Ирганов А.Н.
Date: 2026-10-04
Subject: [PATCH] seL4: framebuffer console for the pc99 debug output

Mirror the kernel/root-task debug output (uart_drv_putchar on pc99) to the
GOP framebuffer reported by GRUB (Multiboot2 type-8 tag -> boot_state.fb_info),
so the boot log is visible on hardware without a serial port (ThinkPad T580).
The kernel window maps all physical memory, so paddr_to_pptr reaches the
framebuffer directly. Serial output is preserved for QEMU -nographic.

diff --git a/src/plat/pc99/machine/io.c b/src/plat/pc99/machine/io.c
index 83a53ba..21f8bdd 100644
--- a/src/plat/pc99/machine/io.c
+++ b/src/plat/pc99/machine/io.c
@@ -34,11 +34,182 @@ void serial_init(uint16_t port)
 /* there is no UART driver at drivers/serial/... for the pc99 platform, but we
  * implement parts of the API here, so we can reuse the generic code.
  */
+
